    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>https://www.andersonmonken.com/authors/anderson/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 16 May 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://www.andersonmonken.com/authors/anderson/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I am passionate about improving policymaking by harnessing the power of data science and artificial intelligence. As the Federal Reserve Board&amp;rsquo;s inaugural Chief AI Officer, I built the Board&amp;rsquo;s AI program from the ground up, leading enterprise AI efforts across technology, adoption, and governance. I manage multiple workstreams to enable responsible and impactful AI use across the organization, advise executive leadership on AI strategy and risk, and represent the Federal Reserve Board in interagency groups and peer CAIO networks. Responsible AI and AI assurance are central to my work, bridging governance and technical practice. My portfolio spans technology leadership, applied research, and teaching. I stay current with the latest developments in AI and actively leverage AI coding tools in my own work. My research includes work on international trade, graph neural networks, and natural language processing. I am experienced with technologies such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, Hadoop, Spark, Impala, spaCy, NLTK, R, and Python.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The views in this website are solely the responsibility of the author and should not be interpreted as reflecting the views of the Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System or of any other person associated with the Federal Reserve System.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
